OL,3,GNEWSAChristmas starts in February for
OL,4,Afestive advert creators
OL,5,
OL,6,FNovember may be associated with darker
OL,7,Fnights and colder weather, but it also
OL,8,Fholds a significant spot on the
OL,9,Fcultural calendar - Christmas advert
OL,10,Fseason. From the sentimental to the
OL,11,Fsilly, high-street brands vie for this
OL,12,Fyear's viral moment, often in the form
OL,13,Fof short films and highly consumable
OL,14,Fcontent, but for the creative minds
OL,15,Fbehind the campaigns, the festive
OL,16,Fperiod starts in February.
OL,18,F"You get January not thinking about
OL,19,FChristmas and then you're sort of back
OL,20,Fin it again. I still love Christmas.
OL,21,FIt's not ruined it for me, thankfully,"
OL,22,FJack Croft jokes.
OL,23,APub: 15-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
